Chapter: Either

 An Either is one of:
   Left -- carries a value of type a.
   Right -- carries a value of type b.

 To is-left gives Boolean, True when the value is Left.
 To is-right gives Boolean, True when the value is Right.
 To from-left gives a, extracting the Left value or returning a default.
 To from-right gives b, extracting the Right value or returning a default.
 To either gives c, eliminating by applying one function to Left or another to Right.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  Either (a) (b) =
    | Left (a)
    | Right (b)

  is-left : Either a b -> Boolean
  is-left (e) = when e
    is Left (x) -> True
    is Right (y) -> False

  is-right : Either a b -> Boolean
  is-right (e) = when e
    is Left (x) -> False
    is Right (y) -> True

  from-left : Either a b, a -> a
  from-left (e) (default) = when e
    is Left (x) -> x
    is Right (y) -> default

  from-right : Either a b, b -> b
  from-right (e) (default) = when e
    is Left (x) -> default
    is Right (y) -> y

  either : (a -> c), (b -> c), Either a b -> c
  either (f) (g) (e) = when e
    is Left (x) -> f x
    is Right (y) -> g y

